// Loops nested deeper than the loop stack held.
//
// push_loop kept its entries in a fixed 32-slot stack and returned
// silently on the 33rd, so a `break` at that depth resolved against the
// enclosing loop instead of its own — it jumped out one level too far.
// Each level here sets its own counter before descending, so every level
// runs exactly once either way and no run can hang; the statement right
// after the innermost loop (inside the enclosing one) is what tells the
// two answers apart: 101 when `break` exits its own loop, 1 when it
// escapes one level too high. deep30 is the control: 30 levels fit in
// the old stack, so it must keep answering 101.
let is i32 as hits with mut = 0;

